 msgctxt "#39961"
-msgid "A 3D Blu-ray holds the picture of each eye as a view of its own (H.264 MVC). Kodi decodes both from a Matroska (MKV) file made of such a disc; a disc, an image of one or a folder of one still plays in 2D. Automatic: both views are decoded, by the processor, where the display says that it takes 3D (it has to be on when Kodi starts), and the video is then shown as a stereoscopic one; on any other display the video plays in 2D as before, with hardware decoding. Always: both views on any display, for anaglyph glasses or for a 3D display that does not say what it is. Off: never. Where the second view cannot be decoded the video plays in 2D. Applies from the next video."
+msgid "A 3D Blu-ray holds the picture of each eye as a view of its own (H.264 MVC). Hades decodes both from a Matroska (MKV) file made of such a disc; a disc, an image of one or a folder of one still plays in 2D. Automatic: both views are decoded, by the processor, where the display says that it takes 3D (it has to be on when Hades starts), and the video is then shown as a stereoscopic one; on any other display the video plays in 2D as before, with hardware decoding. Always: both views on any display, for anaglyph glasses or for a 3D display that does not say what it is. Off: never. Where the second view cannot be decoded the video plays in 2D. Applies from the next video."
 msgstr ""
 
