 #: addons/skin.estuary/xml/Variables.xml
@@ -1380,7 +1380,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 #. Setting help of #31711
 msgctxt "#31712"
-msgid "For a 3D TV or projector. While Kodi draws in a split 3D mode (over/under or side by side), the display is told so over HDMI and switches to 3D by itself. Frame packing, which keeps both eyes at full resolution, is used where the display and the graphics driver have it (Kodi then draws over/under, also for a side-by-side video); else the half format that is drawn. The refresh rate is the one the video gets anyway: for a film in frame packing, turn on the adjustment of the display's refresh rate to the video, because HDMI has frame packing for 1080p at 24 Hz only. The display has to be on when Kodi starts. Expect one more change of display mode when a 3D video starts and when it stops. Off: the two halves go out as an ordinary 2D picture and the display is switched to 3D by hand. Turn it off if a 3D video shows a black or broken picture. Without a 3D display nothing changes. Applies the next time the display mode is set."
+msgid "For a 3D TV or projector. While Hades draws in a split 3D mode (over/under or side by side), the display is told so over HDMI and switches to 3D by itself. Frame packing, which keeps both eyes at full resolution, is used where the display and the graphics driver have it (Hades then draws over/under, also for a side-by-side video); else the half format that is drawn. The refresh rate is the one the video gets anyway: for a film in frame packing, turn on the adjustment of the display's refresh rate to the video, because HDMI has frame packing for 1080p at 24 Hz only. The display has to be on when Hades starts. Expect one more change of display mode when a 3D video starts and when it stops. Off: the two halves go out as an ordinary 2D picture and the display is switched to 3D by hand. Turn it off if a 3D video shows a black or broken picture. Without a 3D display nothing changes. Applies the next time the display mode is set."
 msgstr ""
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
@@ -1392,5 +1392,17 @@ msgstr ""
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 #. Setting help of #31721
 msgctxt "#31722"
-msgid "A 3D Blu-ray holds the picture of each eye as a view of its own (H.264 MVC). Kodi decodes both from a Matroska (MKV) file made of such a disc; a disc, an image of one or a folder of one still plays in 2D. Automatic: both views are decoded, by the processor, where the display says that it takes 3D (it has to be on when Kodi starts), and the video is then shown as a stereoscopic one; on any other display the video plays in 2D as before, with hardware decoding. Always: both views on any display, for anaglyph glasses or for a 3D display that does not say what it is. Off: never. Where the second view cannot be decoded the video plays in 2D. Applies from the next video."
+msgid "A 3D Blu-ray holds the picture of each eye as a view of its own (H.264 MVC). Hades decodes both from a Matroska (MKV) file made of such a disc; a disc, an image of one or a folder of one still plays in 2D. Automatic: both views are decoded, by the processor, where the display says that it takes 3D (it has to be on when Hades starts), and the video is then shown as a stereoscopic one; on any other display the video plays in 2D as before, with hardware decoding. Always: both views on any display, for anaglyph glasses or for a 3D display that does not say what it is. Off: never. Where the second view cannot be decoded the video plays in 2D. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr ""
+
