diff --git a/privacy-policy.txt b/privacy-policy.txt
index 3c88971..1dce1ba 100644
--- a/privacy-policy.txt
+++ b/privacy-policy.txt
@@ -1,3 +1,27 @@
+[B]LibreELEC Hades: privacy[/B]
+
+LibreELEC Hades is a modified build of LibreELEC and of Kodi. It is not supplied by, endorsed by or a product of the XBMC Foundation, and what follows this note is not a promise of whoever made this build: it is Kodi's own privacy policy, kept as Kodi publishes it, because the media centre here is Kodi with changes and uses the same services.
+
+What this build adds to it:
+
+    • It sends nothing to those who make it. It has no telemetry and sends no usage statistics, it does not look for updates of the system (it has no place yet to ask), and its makers run no server.
+    • Its diagnostics are off unless you turn them on, and what they save stays on your drive.
+
+What it contacts without being asked, as Kodi and LibreELEC do:
+
+    • When a network comes up, the system fetches a page of the ConnMan project (ipv4.connman.net or ipv6.connman.net) to know whether it reaches the internet, and it sets its clock by the servers of pool.ntp.org unless your network or you name others. If your network gives it no name server, it asks Google's (8.8.8.8 and 8.8.4.4).
+    • Kodi looks for updates of the add-ons that are installed and installs them, from the add-on repositories of Kodi (mirrors.kodi.tv) and of LibreELEC (addons.libreelec.tv). A setting in Settings, System, Add-ons turns that off.
+
+What it contacts when you use it:
+
+    • If you make a library of films, series or music, the information providers that come with Kodi ask their services for what they show: The Movie Database, fanart.tv, TheAudioDB, MusicBrainz, AllMusic and others.
+    • If you play an audio CD, Kodi asks gnudb.org for its titles. A setting in Settings, Player, Discs turns that off.
+    • If you tell the settings of LibreELEC to send a log (System, Submit Log), the log goes to the paste service of LibreELEC (paste.libreelec.tv) and is kept there under the address that you are shown. Nothing is sent before you choose that.
+    • Whatever the add-ons that you install contact.
+
+Those servers see your network address and what the program that asks says of itself. The media centre says "Kodi" with its version and "LibreELEC" with its own: to them this build looks like Kodi on LibreELEC. Their own privacy policies apply to that.
+
+
 [B]Kodi Privacy Policy[/B]
 [I]2016 Oct 23[/I]
 
